The '''Leader of the Christian Socialist Union (Burawa)''' is the highest-ranking position within the [[Christian Socialist Union (Burawa)|Christian Socialist Union]], responsible for setting party policy, representing the party in public, and serving as the party's candidate for [[Leader of the Burawi Republic]] in leadership elections.

The position was established on 5 April 1996 when the Christian Socialist Union split from the [[National Party of Burawa]] in opposition to the [[Domestic Partnership Act of 1996 (Burawa)|Domestic Partnership Act of 1996]].

